# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / Cargo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. Not just the root one: `target/` matches at any depth, so a
# crate that is built from its own directory is covered too. This is the
# single biggest thing that must never reach the index -- `app/target/` was
# 4.6 GB, and staging it is what left the repository with a broken,
# half-written object store and failing periodic commits.
/target/
target/
**/target/
/target2/
target2/
**/target2/

# Rust build artifacts and tooling output
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.wasm
*.wat

# Cargo.lock IS tracked for the app crate (it is a binary/application crate).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled binaries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.out
*.app
*.com
*.bin
*.msi
*.msix
*.deb
*.rpm
*.apk
*.appimage
*.jar
*.war

# Native/compiled helper output that lives beside sources
/app/check_png.exe
/app/check_png.pdb

